    {
      "object_id": "mathia_interpretation_b205a3ffdf4a07022ce94df9f2e42593cebd6b1dbac71f9be97ed1683a817db8",
      "object_role": "interpretation",
      "proposed_content": "The common degree-2g numerator makes functional equation, rationality, and pRH three distinct proof targets. Its value is diagnostic: symmetry and finite presentation can be established without thereby settling the quantitative modulus condition. Historically Schmidt supplied the first two, whereas the cited pRH result was elliptic, so arbitrary genus remained the proof burden; this separation does not claim formal logical independence.",
