    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_3ab5599a142d765c8e7ccaca0cc14ce9000f2adff962a51aa28857ec73f8269c",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Across the source, finite-field zeta information is successively organized as Artin's finite root-modulus problem, the complete-curve rational numerator with Frobenius factors, extension-field counts recovered as their power sums, and, in genus one, a Frobenius endomorphism whose norm identity yields pRH.",
