    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_f31aced9f24134d7050f4c1d37a4709313d52c2823c3cc4791778c11f9db51da",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Deuring's proposed higher-genus generalization preserves the algebraic role of Hasse's elliptic endomorphism ring by replacing it with the ring of self-correspondences, but Hasse's own program makes clear that constructing this ring leaves essential differential and norm theories missing before the anticipated positivity reduction can address pRH.",
